**EXCERPT FROM THE EXTRACTION AND PROCESSING AGREEMENT**

**THIS EXTRACTION AND PROCESSING AGREEMENT** ("Agreement") is made and entered into as of the 15th day of March, 2023, by and between:

1. **Green Earth Mining, LLC** ("GEM"), a limited liability company organized and existing under the laws of the State of Colorado, with its principal office located at 1234 Mineral Way, Denver, CO 80202, hereinafter referred to as "Contractor".

2. **Bright Future Industries, Inc.** ("BFI"), a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of California, with its principal office located at 5678 Innovation Drive, San Jose, CA 95134, hereinafter referred to as "Client".

**RECITALS**

WHEREAS, the Client is engaged in the sustainable production and processing of mineral resources and seeks to engage the Contractor for the extraction, processing, and compliance activities associated with mineral extraction operations at the site located at 4555 Resource Lane, Nevada County, California (the "Site");

WHEREAS, the Contractor possesses the necessary expertise, personnel, and equipment to perform the extraction and processing services in accordance with applicable environmental laws and regulations;

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements herein contained, the parties agree as follows:

**ARTICLE I: DEFINITIONS**

1.1 "Extraction Services" shall mean the activities performed by Contractor related to the removal of mineral resources from the Site, including, but not limited to, drilling, blasting, hauling, and loading.

1.2 "Processing Services" shall mean the activities performed by Contractor related to the refinement and processing of extracted minerals, including, but not limited to, crushing, milling, and chemical treatment.

1.3 "Environmental Compliance" shall mean adherence to all applicable federal, state, and local laws, regulations, and permits governing environmental protection and natural resource management.

1.4 "Equipment" shall mean all machinery, tools, vehicles, and related items utilized by the Contractor in the performance of Extraction and Processing Services, including but not limited to CAT 789D haul trucks, Komatsu PC5500 excavators, and Metso HP300 crushers.

1.5 "Permits" shall mean all necessary licenses, approvals, and authorizations required for the performance of Extraction and Processing Services, including but not limited to, permits issued by the California Department of Conservation and the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency.

**ARTICLE II: SCOPE OF SERVICES**

2.1 The Contractor agrees to provide Extraction Services and Processing Services as detailed in Schedule A attached hereto.

2.2 The Contractor shall utilize the Equipment listed in Schedule B for the performance of the services.

2.3 The Contractor shall ensure that all operations conducted at the Site comply with the Environmental Compliance requirements set forth in Article V.

**ARTICLE III: COMPENSATION AND PAYMENT**

3.1 The Client shall pay the Contractor a fee of $3,500,000, payable in installments based on milestones as defined in Schedule C.

3.2 Payments shall be made within thirty (30) days of receipt of an invoice from the Contractor detailing the services rendered, including any supporting documentation as required.

3.3 Late payments shall incur interest at the rate of 1.5% per month.

**ARTICLE IV: DURATION**

4.1 This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and shall continue for a period of three (3) years, unless terminated earlier in accordance with Article XIV.

4.2 The Client may extend the term of this Agreement for two (2) additional one-year periods upon written notice to the Contractor at least ninety (90) days prior to the expiration of the Initial Term.

**ARTICLE V: ENVIRONMENTAL COMPLIANCE**

5.1 The Contractor shall conduct all activities in accordance with applicable local, state, and federal environmental laws and regulations, including, but not limited to, the California Environmental Quality Act (CEQA) and the National Environmental Policy Act (NEPA).

5.2 The Contractor shall maintain all necessary Permits and provide copies to the Client upon request.

5.3 The Contractor shall develop and implement an Environmental Management Plan (EMP) in coordination with the Client, to include measures for waste management, air quality control, and water usage efficiency.

5.4 The Contractor shall notify the Client within twenty-four (24) hours of any environmental incidents or regulatory violations occurring during the performance of the services.

**ARTICLE VI: EQUIPMENT AND MAINTENANCE**

6.1 The Contractor shall be responsible for the procurement, operation, maintenance, and repair of all Equipment required to perform the services.

6.2 The Contractor shall adhere to the maintenance schedules provided by the manufacturers of the Equipment, including but not limited to Caterpillar, Komatsu, and Metso.

6.3 The Contractor shall maintain records of all maintenance and repairs performed on the Equipment and provide such records to the Client upon request.

6.4 The Client shall have the right to inspect the Equipment at any reasonable time and may require the Contractor to replace any Equipment that is deemed inadequate or unsafe.

**ARTICLE VII: PERSONNEL**

7.1 The Contractor shall employ qualified personnel, including but not limited to:

- **Jake Thompson**, Project Manager
- **Emily Ramirez**, Environmental Compliance Officer
- **Michael Chen**, Lead Engineer
- **Sophia Patel**, Geologist

7.2 The Contractor shall ensure that all personnel undergo training and certification as required by applicable laws and regulations, including OSHA standards.

7.3 The Contractor shall provide the Client with a list of all personnel working at the Site, including their qualifications and roles.

**ARTICLE VIII: INDEMNIFICATION AND INSURANCE**

8.1 The Contractor agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Client and its officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any and all claims, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or related to the performance of this Agreement, except to the extent caused by the negligence or willful misconduct of the Client.

8.2 The Contractor shall maintain insurance coverage throughout the term of this Agreement, including:

- General liability insurance with a limit of not less than $5,000,000 per occurrence.
- Workers' compensation insurance as required by applicable law.
- Environmental liability insurance with a limit of not less than $2,000,000.

8.3 Certificates of insurance shall be provided to the Client within ten (10) days of the Effective Date and upon renewal of each policy thereafter.

**ARTICLE IX: HEALTH AND SAFETY**

9.1 The Contractor shall implement a Health and Safety Plan (HASP) to minimize risks associated with mining operations, including training programs and regular safety meetings.

9.2 The Contractor shall ensure compliance with all applicable health and safety laws and regulations, including those enforced by the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA).

9.3 The Contractor is responsible for providing personal protective equipment (PPE) to all personnel working on the Site.

**ARTICLE X: TERMINATION**

10.1 Either party may terminate this Agreement for cause upon written notice if the other party fails to perform any material obligation under this Agreement and such failure continues for a period of thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice of default.

10.2 The Client may terminate this Agreement without cause upon ninety (90) days’ written notice to the Contractor.

10.3 Upon termination, the Contractor shall cease all activities and submit a final invoice for services rendered up to the date of termination.

**ARTICLE XI: CONFIDENTIALITY**

11.1 Both parties agree to maintain the confidentiality of all proprietary and confidential information received from the other party during the term of this Agreement.

11.2 Confidential information shall not include information that is publicly known or becomes publicly known through no fault of the receiving party.

11.3 The obligations of confidentiality shall survive the termination of this Agreement for a period of five (5) years.

**ARTICLE XII: DISPUTE RESOLUTION**

12.1 Any dispute arising from or related to this Agreement shall be resolved by binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association.

12.2 The arbitration shall take place in Denver, Colorado, and shall be conducted by a single arbitrator with experience in mining and environmental law.

**ARTICLE XIII: MISCELLANEOUS**

13.1 This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes all prior agreements and understandings, whether written or oral.

13.2 This Agreement may not be amended or modified except in writing signed by both parties.

13.3 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Colorado.

