**ARTICLE XXXIII: DISPUTE RESOLUTION**

33.1 **Negotiation**: In the event of any dispute arising out of or relating to this Agreement, the parties shall first attempt to resolve the dispute through good faith negotiations between the designated representatives of both parties.

33.2 **Mediation**: If the dispute is not resolved within [insert number] days through negotiation, the parties agree to submit to mediation conducted by a mutually agreed-upon mediator. The mediation shall be held in [insert location], and each party shall bear its own costs of mediation.

33.3 **Arbitration**: If the dispute remains unresolved after mediation, either party may submit the dispute to binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the [insert arbitration association, e.g., American Arbitration Association]. The arbitration shall take place in [insert location], and the decision of the arbitrator(s) shall be final and binding on both parties. Each party shall be responsible for its own legal fees and costs associated with the arbitration.

33.4 **Confidentiality of Dispute Resolution**: Any negotiations, mediations, or arbitrations conducted pursuant to this Article shall be confidential, and neither party shall disclose the existence or results of such proceedings without the prior written consent of the other party, unless required by law.

